    File content: {"language": "python", "module_docstring": "Motivation of this design (instead of using mlflow directly):\n- Better design than mlflow native design\n    - we have record object with a lot of methods(more intuitive), instead of use run_id everytime in mlflow\n        - So the recorder's interfaces like log, start, will be more intuitive.\n- Provide richer and tailerd features than mlflow native\n    - Logging code diff at the start of run.\n    - log_object and load_object to for Python object directly instead log_artifact and download_artifact\n- (weak) Allow diverse backend support\n\nTo be honest, design always add burdens. For example,\n- You need to create an experiment before you can get a recorder. (In MLflow, experiments are more like tags, and you often just use a run_id in many interfaces without first defining an experiment.)", "imports": ["contextlib.contextmanager", "typing.Text", "typing.Optional", "typing.Any", "typing.Dict", "expm.ExpManager", "exp.Experiment", "recorder.Recorder", "utils.Wrapper", "utils.exceptions.RecorderInitializationError", "sys"], "constants": ["R: QlibRecorderWrapper"], "functions": [], "async_functions": [], "classes": [{"class_name": "QlibRecorder", "decorators": [], "bases": [], "attributes": [], "methods": ["__init__(self, exp_manager: ExpManager)", "__repr__(self)", "start(self, experiment_id: Optional[Text], experiment_name: Optional[Text], recorder_id: Optional[Text], recorder_name: Optional[Text], uri: Optional[Text], resume: bool)", "start_exp(self, experiment_id, experiment_name, recorder_id, recorder_name, uri, resume)", "end_exp(self, recorder_status)", "search_records(self, experiment_ids, **kwargs)", "list_experiments(self)", "list_recorders(self, experiment_id, experiment_name)", "get_exp(self, experiment_id, experiment_name, create: bool, start: bool) -> Experiment", "delete_exp(self, experiment_id, experiment_name)", "get_uri(self)", "set_uri(self, uri: Optional[Text])", "uri_context(self, ur